std, unwind, backtrace: the EmiBSD target

Why a patch: the standard library selects its platform code by target_os,
and EmiBSD's libc presents the same interface as OpenBSD's (D-0003: the ABI
kept byte-identical). `target_os = "emibsd"` joins every condition that
names "openbsd" in std, unwind and backtrace (futex(2), arc4random, the
stack-guard query through pthread_stackseg_np, getthrid, the socket options,
the file-system calls, dl_iterate_phdr for backtraces, libc++abi for the
unwinder); what carries the system's name is EmiBSD's own: std::os::emibsd
(the raw types and MetadataExt, as std::os::openbsd has them),
std::env::consts::OS = "emibsd", the target_os list of std's build script;
the unwinder links libunwind too, because DevTools builds libc++abi over
LLVM's libunwind as a library of its own. Written by EmiBSD (ISC) over
upstream's text (Apache-2.0 OR MIT), carried by DevTools over the pinned
tag, offered upstream when stable. Author: Emilio Navarrete Lineros,
2026-10-31.

